# This working tree is shared between macOS and Windows checkouts over OneDrive,
# so line endings must not depend on whichever device last wrote a file.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF, the sync layer carries them to the Mac, and every tracked file
# then reads as locally modified. Observed 2026-07-24: a fresh Windows clone
# showed all 68 tracked files changed, none of them actually edited.
#
# LF everywhere also keeps bin/*.sh and the doctor scripts runnable, and lets
# patches/*.patch apply cleanly with `git apply` (which is whitespace-sensitive).
#
# text=auto rather than a blanket `text` so a binary added later is detected and
# left alone instead of being corrupted by newline translation.
* text=auto eol=lf
